{title: 403 - Let Us Break Bread Together}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Gm]Let [Cm/G]us break bread together [Fm/Ab]on [Cm/G]our [Ab]knees,
[Eb/Bb]Let [Fm]us [Gm]break bread together [Am]on [Bb]our [Cm]knees.
[Cm/G]When [Gm]I fall on [C/E]my [Edim]knees [Fm]with my face [Bb7]to [Bb]the rising [Ab]sun,
[Fm/Ab]OLord, [Ab]have [Fm]mercy [Eb/G]onme.

Verse 2:
[Gm]Let [Cm/G]us drink wine together [Fm/Ab]on [Cm/G]our [Ab]knees,
[Eb/Bb]let [Fm]us [Gm]drink wine together [Am]on [Bb]our [Cm]knees.
[Cm/G]When [Gm]I fall on [C/E]my [Edim]knees [Fm]with my face [Bb7]to [Bb]the rising [Ab]sun,
[Fm/Ab]O Lord, [Ab]have [Fm]mercy [Ab]on [Eb/G]me.

Verse 3:
[Gm]Let [Cm/G]us praise God together [Fm/Ab]on [Cm/G]our [Ab]knees,
[Eb/Bb]let [Fm]us [Gm]praise God together [Am]on [Bb]our [Cm]knees.
[Cm/G]When [Gm]I fall on [C/E]my [Edim]knees [Fm]with my face [Bb7]to [Bb]the rising [Ab]sun,
[Fm/Ab]O Lord, [Ab]have [Fm]mercy [Ab]on [Eb/G]me.
